{
  "about": "Bengali (Bangla, as read in West Bengal) glossary for drharshmaheshwari.com. Every Bengali translation must use these terms: tests/i18n.test.mjs checks that when an English text contains a term, its Bengali has one of the accepted forms (substring match, so a stem shared by every inflection is listed). Change a term here, then retranslate what uses it. docs/translation.md has the rules.",
  "register": "Everyday spoken (chalit) Bangla that a family in Kolkata would use, not sadhu bhasha or textbook Sanskritised words. Common English health words that people say in Bangla stay as they are said (BMI, ব্লাড সুগার, ডায়াবেটিস, ব্লাড প্রেশার). Polite আপনি form. Short sentences ending in '।'. Numbers in 0-9, never Bengali digits. Units as in English (cm, kg).",
